[1787308935309] [note] #93 HOSTILE PROXIMITY CENSUS -- the HOSTILE half of the encounter.
[1787308935309] [note] 
[1787308935309] [note] WHY THIS ARM EXISTS. Items 14 (Guard) and 15 (Fortifications) are blocked on
[1787308935309] [note] one unmeasured fact. Every ARC 3 arm reads identically: a hostile spawns,
[1787308935309] [note] by_target=true FLEE emits fire, health=1.0 on every colonist, zero damage
[1787308935310] [note] lines. THREE stories fit that equally well:
[1787308935310] [note] S1 flight works -- separation opens faster than the wolf closes it
[1787308935310] [note] S2 it never pursues -- the wolf never selects a colonist
[1787308935310] [note] S3 it reaches but cannot harm
[1787308935310] [note] Nothing on disk separates them, because NOTHING HAS EVER MEASURED THE
[1787308935310] [note] WOLF. This arm is a measurement, not a fixture.
[1787308935310] [note] 
[1787308935310] [note] ★ WHAT #92 COST AND WHAT IT BOUGHT. Four VOIDs went into building a TRAP to
[1787308935310] [note] defeat S1 by removing escape. The fifth reading proved the trap
[1787308935310] [note] impossible: the engine plans a ladder BEFORE releasing deep cells, so a
[1787308935310] [note] shaft either holds nobody (gate closed) or has a way out (gate open).
[1787308935310] [note] A shaft cannot trap a WORKING colonist. Hence: instrument instead.
[1787308935310] [note] 
[1787308935310] [note] ★★ THE FIXTURE IS DELIBERATELY THE PLAINEST ONE AVAILABLE -- flat, resourced,
[1787308935310] [note] no pit, no shaft, no wall. Every geometric variable that voided an earlier
[1787308935310] [note] attempt is simply absent. The only event is the spawn.
[1787308935310] [note] 
[1787308935310] [note] THE INSTRUMENT: server-side `bastion: hostile proximity census`, every 30
[1787308935310] [note] ticks, gated on BASTION_HOSTILE_PROXIMITY_DIAG. The client samples below
[1787308935310] [note] are WITNESSES that colonists are alive and ticking -- they are NOT the
[1787308935310] [note] measurement (item 13c: 40 of 40 client samples read drive=Work while the
[1787308935310] [note] server emitted Flee twice).
